{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790194756,"nonce":"Dp8tgRkp5jUIH5WOlS2FM6flz2w=","title":"Found by the two-clone config push/pull test while building entities/config (3556569). On the diverged merge path (dag scenario 5) MergeAll returns the local entity as read before the merge commit, so SubCache.MergeAll cached an excerpt holding only the local history; the ref hash recorded beside it was the merged one, so the staleness diff (d591cb3) saw nothing wrong and the bad excerpt survived every reopen. Affected bugs and issues equally. entity/dag is pristine, so the fix is in cache/subcache.go: re-read the entity from the refs after the merge instead of trusting what the merge returned. Fixed in dd531a0f with a regression test (TestConfigPushPull).","message":"","files":null}]}